(Let's outline:)
(Phase A: Alpha early steps up to apply_operational_constraint (including attach_task_profile, confirm_candidate_preparedness, assign_operator_resource, apply_operational_constraint, confirm_operator_alignment). After that we can detach task profile.)
(Phase B: Prepare origin and destination availability (create, allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness, activate node, assign operator, lock). This will use task profile for origin and destination sequentially; we can do origin then destination, each time attaching, preparing, locking, then detaching to free for next.)
(Phase C: Assemble transport leg, authorize loading, load container for alpha, stage, verify loading profile, establish clearance, attach service window.)
(Phase D: Reattach task profile to alpha, validate route sequence, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch.)
(Phase E: Dispatch origin and destination (mark dispatch ready, allocate dispatch slot, execute dispatch) – note we already allocated dispatch slots for origin/destination in phase B? Actually we haven't yet; we need to allocate dispatch slots and execute dispatch for origin/destination. We can do that after they are locked)
